<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 69 0 R
/T (Delinquency rates increased across four of the five major property types, led by lodging and retail, while multifamily was unchanged. Lodging increased 49 basis points to 5.84% after newly delinquent balances from the New Orleans hotel and a national hotel portfolio exceeded the impact of a smaller group of cures. Retail followed with a 24-basis-point increase to 7.20%, driven by newly delinquent regional malls that outweighed cures among other malls returning to performing matured balloon status.)
/E (Delinquency rates increased across four of the five major property types, led by lodging and retail, while multifamily was unchanged. Lodging increased 49 basis points to 5.84% after newly delinquent balances from the New Orleans hotel and a national hotel portfolio exceeded the impact of a smaller group of cures. Retail followed with a 24-basis-point increase to 7.20%, driven by newly delinquent regional malls that outweighed cures among other malls returning to performing matured balloon status.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
87 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 69 0 R
/T (The office rate rose nine basis points to 12.00% as the large newly delinquent loans described above more than offset two sizable loans that left delinquency, including one that resolved directly from foreclosure. Industrial increased one basis point to 1.14% on limited newly delinquent volume. Multifamily held at 7.69% as new 30-day delinquencies across several states were balanced by a similarly broad group of cures.)
/E (The office rate rose nine basis points to 12.00% as the large newly delinquent loans described above more than offset two sizable loans that left delinquency, including one that resolved directly from foreclosure. Industrial increased one basis point to 1.14% on limited newly delinquent volume. Multifamily held at 7.69% as new 30-day delinquencies across several states were balanced by a similarly broad group of cures.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
