/Title (Delinquency rates increased across four of the five major property types, led by lodging and retail, while multifamily was unchanged. Lodging increased 49 basis points to 5.84% after newly delinquent balances from the New Orleans hotel and a national hotel portfolio exceeded the impact of a smaller group of cures. Retail followed with a 24-basis-point increase to 7.20%, driven by newly delinquent regional malls that outweighed cures among other malls returning to performing matured balloon status.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 502 0 R
/Prev 580 0 R
/Next 609 0 R
>>
endobj
